{"id":"word:hebrew:H3844","type":"word","title":"לְבָנוֹן","subtitle":"H3844 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Lebanon , a mountain range in Palestine","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לְבָנוֹן (H3844) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-loc.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 71 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לְבָנוֹן (Lᵉbânôwn) means Lebanon , a mountain range in Palestine First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 5 13."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לְבָנוֹן","transliteration":"Lᵉbânôwn","pronunciation":"leb-aw-nohn'","strong":"H3844","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3844","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-loc","forms":["הַ/לְּבָנוֹן֙","הַ/לְּבָנֽוֹן","לְבָנ֑וֹן","הַ/לְּבָנ֔וֹן","לְבָנ֖וֹן"],"morphs":[["HTd/Np",25],["HNp",17],["HRd/Np",15],["HC/Td/Np",5],["HR/Np",3],["HC/Rd/Np",2],["HC/Np",2],["HNp/Sd",1],["HR/Td/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Lebanon , a mountain range in Palestine","usage":"Lebanon.","full":"H3844. Lebanon לְבָנוֺן ( Deut 3:25 הַלְּבָנֹן van d. H.) 71 proper name, of a mountain Lebanon (Phoenician לבנן ; Assyrian Labnanu , etc., Schr COT on 1Kin 5:13 , Dl Par. 103 ff. ; Egyptian Ra-m­n-n WMM Asien u.Europa,197ff. ; Arabic compare further Rob BR ii, 435ff. 493GASm Geogr.45ff. Buhl Geogr.110 and references ; name probably from whiteness of its cliffs Rob BR ii, 493 ); — wooded mountain-range on northern border of Israel [usually with article ׳הַלּ (51 t.); without article לְבָנוֺן , in poetry and late Hosea 14:8 ; Nahum 1:4 ; 2Kin 19:23 = Isa 37:24 ; Ezek 31:15-16 , Isa 14:8 ; 29:17 ; 33:9 ; 40:16 ; Jer 18:14 ; Hab 2:17 ; Zech 10:10 ; 11:1 ; Psa 29:6 ; Song 4:8 (twice in verse); 4:11 , 15 ; with ה locative לְבָב֫וֺנָה 1 Kings 5:28a]; perhaps first mentioned in defining a locality, as הַלְּבָנוֺן הַר , Judg 3:3 (E according to GFM; this combination only here), but also in early prophets, then in D, and later; — in defining a locality Josh 9:1 ; הַלּ ׳בִּקְעַת 11:17 ; 12:7 (side of Baal Gad); as a marked feature, in describing extent of land Deut 1:7 ; 3:25 ; 11:24 ; Josh 1:4 ; 13:5 ( כָּלהַֿל ) 13:6 (all D), 1Kin 9:19 2Chr 8:6 ; Jer 22:26 ; Zech 10:10 ; ׳אשׁהַל׳ר Jer 22:6 (figurative of royal house of Judah), as a height Song 4:8 (twice in verse); הַל ׳מִגְדַּל Cant 7:5 i.e. a tower built on Lebanon; ל ׳שֶׁלֶג Jer 18:14 snow of L. ; L. as source of streams Song 4:15 ; ל ׳יֵין Hosea 14:8 ; most often, however, as bearing forests, especially of cedars, הַלּ ׳אַרְזֵי Judg 9:15 (in allegory; perhaps J, according to GFM), Isa 2:13 ; 14:8 ; Psa 29:5 ; 104:16 , compare 1Kin 5:13 ; 1 Kings 5:20; 1 Kings 5:23; 1 Kings 5:28 (twice in verse); 2Chr 2:7 (twice in verse); 2:15 , 2Kin 14:9 (twice in verse) = 2Chr 25:18 (twice in verse) (in allegory), Jer 22:23 ; Ezek 17:3 ; 27:5 ; 31:3 , 15 , 16 ; Zech 11:1 ; Ezra 3:7 ; Psa 92:13 ; Song 3:9 ; 5:15 (simile of majestic figure); ל ׳מֶּרַח Nahum 1:4 ; הַלּ ׳כְּבוֺד Isa 35:2 ; 60:13 ; ל ׳וְשָׁב לְכַרְמֶל 29:17 ׅ || ל ׳יַרְכְּתֵי (יַעַר with the same reference 37:24 = 2Kin 19:23 ; ׳הַלּ = trees of Lebanon Hosea 14:6 ; Isa 10:34 ; 40:16 ; Psa 29:6 ; 72:16 ; ׳ל Isa 33:9 figurative, as mourning; ל ׳חֲמַס Hab 2:17 i.e. violence done to Lebanon , probably by cutting down its trees; הַלּ יַעַר ׳בֵּית a royal mansion of Solomon, 1Kin 7:2 ; and 10:17 , 21 2Chr 9:16 , 20 ; ׳ל as home of wild beast 2Kin 14:9 2Chr 25:18 (in allegory); לְבָנוֺן רֵיחַ , of the odour of cedar forests Song 4:11 , compare Hosea 14:7 (in simile; We thinks ׳ל here to be a specific plant).","rootNote":"from 3825 ; (the) white mountain (from its snow);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 5 13","keyReferences":["1Kgs 5 13","1Kgs 5 20","1Kgs 5 23","1Kgs 5 28","1Kgs 5 28","1Kgs 7 2","1Kgs 9 19","1Kgs 10 17"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":71,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 5 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"ve